  "Oath-Scroll of the Styx":{sp:"Oath of the Styx",lore:"The gods swear by the black river, and if they break that oath they sleep for a great year and are cast out of heaven for nine more. The scroll is wet. It has been wet for a very long time."},
  "Siren's Songbook":{sp:"Siren Song",lore:"Notation for a song that is not meant to be sung by a mouth. Each line drops a half-step lower than the one before. The last line is a rest. It is the loudest part."},
  "Codex of the Drowned Court":{sp:"Drowning Crown",lore:"The household book of a king who ruled below the tide line. It lists his courtiers, his debts, and the price of a crown of black water. Salt crystals crust the binding."},
